rate sidebar destination."},{"markdown":"The picker is a flex-wrap **chip grid** (driven by `PROVIDER_CARDS` in [[src/renderer/src/constants.ts]]) rather than a dropdown: every native provider is a chip, and a terminal `local` (\"Local / Others\") chip reveals the `LOCAL_PRESETS` rows (local servers + remote OpenAI-compatible endpoints). `selectProvider` is the shared click handler for the provider chips and the preset chips.","startLine":31,"endLine":31,"text":"The picker is a flex-wrap chip grid (driven by PROVIDER_CARDS in src/renderer/src/constants.ts) rather than a dropdown: every native provider is a chip, and a terminal local (\"Local / Others\") chip reveals the LOCAL_PRESETS rows (local servers + remote OpenAI-compatible endpoints). selectProvider is the shared click handler for the provider chips and the preset chips."},{"markdown":"Once a provider is configured the grid collapses to a read-only summary (logo + provider label + model/base-URL); a **Change** button in the section header (`editingProvider` state) re-opens the full chip grid and the editable model/base-URL fields. An unconfigured (`auto`) selection always shows the grid.","startLine":33,"endLine":33,"text":"Once a provider is configured the grid collapses to a read-only summary (logo + provider label + model/base-URL); a Change button in the section header (editingProvider state) re-opens the full chip grid and the editable model/base-URL fields. An unconfigured (auto) selection always shows the grid."},{"markdown":"For compatible/custom endpoints, an inline **API Key** field appears under Base URL, stored under the host-derived env var (`resolveCompatEnvKey`: preset `envKey` else `expectedEnvKeyForUrl`, e.g. AtlasCloud → `ATLASCLOUD_API_KEY`). It shares the `env` state with the lower LLM-provider key cards, so either entry point stays in sync.","startLine":35,"endLine":35,"text":"For compatible/custom endpoints, an inline API Key field appears under Base URL, stored under the host-derived env var (resolveCompatEnvKey: preset envKey else expectedEnvKeyForUrl, e.g. AtlasCloud → ATLASCLOUD_API_KEY). It shares the env state with the lower LLM-provider key cards, so either entry point stays in sync."},{"markdown":"Ids the agent can't resolve by id are listed in `OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_BASE_URLS` ([[src/renderer/src/constants.ts]]) — openai, perplexity, and every `LOCAL_PRESETS` chip (local servers + remote endpoints like groq, deepseek, atlascloud, mistral, …). This map MUST contain every preset id, or selecting that chip mis-routes; a test in `tests/constants.test.ts` enforces it. Selecting one autofills its base URL and shows the base-URL field; on save it is persisted as `provider: custom` + `base_url`, which the gateway accepts and uses to host-derive the API key (`runtime_provider._host_derived_api_key`, e.g. `api.groq.com` → `GROQ_API_KEY`). `displayProviderFromConfig` reverse-maps a stored `custom` + known base URL back to the brand id so the dropdown re-selects it on load. Native providers (the gateway hardcodes their base URL) clear the field instead.","startLine":37,"endLine":37,"text":"Ids the agent can't resolve by id are listed in OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_BASE_URLS (src/renderer/src/constants.ts) — openai, perplexity, and every LOCAL_PRESETS chip (local servers + remote endpoints like groq, deepseek, atlascloud, mistral, …). This map MUST contain every preset id, or selecting that chip mis-routes; a test in tests/constants.test.ts enforces it. Selecting one autofills its base URL and shows the base-URL field; on save it is persisted as provider: custom + base_url, which the gateway accepts and uses to host-derive the API key (runtime_provider._host_derived_api_key, e.g. api.groq.com → GROQ_API_KEY). displayProviderFromConfig reverse-maps a stored custom + known base URL back to the brand id so the dropdown re-selects it on load. Native providers (the gateway hardcodes their base URL) clear the field instead."},{"markdown":"Activating a model must rewrite or clear `model.api_mode`, or a stale protocol from the previous model routes the new endpoint over the wrong transport — dropping connections when switching OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible custom endpoints.","startLine":41,"endLine":41,"text":"Activating a model must rewrite or clear model.api_mode, or a stale protocol from the previous model routes the new endpoint over the wrong transport — dropping connections when switching OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible custom endpoints."},{"markdown":"The gateway's runtime-provider resolver honors a persisted `model.api_mode` (`anthropic_messages` vs `chat_completions`, …) for `custom`/compatible providers, and only auto-detects from the base URL (`/anthropic` suffix, `api.openai.com`, …) when the key is absent. So a leftover `anthropic_messages` would keep an OpenAI-compatible endpoint pointed at `/v1/messages` (404 / lost connection).","startLine":43,"endLine":43,"text":"The gateway's runtime-provider resolver honors a persisted model.api_mode (anthropic_messages vs chat_completions, …) for custom/compatible providers, and only auto-detects from the base URL (/anthropic suffix, api.openai.com, …) when the key is absent. So a leftover anthropic_messages would keep an OpenAI-compatible endpoint pointed at /v1/messages (404 / lost connection)."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/config.ts#setModelConfig]] takes an optional `apiMode` argument, handled exactly like `context_length`: a non-empty string sets `model.api_mode`, `null`/empty removes it (so auto-detection resumes), `undefined` leaves it untouched. The `set-model-config` IPC handler ([[src/main/ipc/register.ts]]) resolves it from the activated model's `apiMode` library field ([[src/main/models.ts#SavedModel]]) — `null` when the entry has none — alongside the `contextLength` mirror, on both the pure-local and remote-fallback local writes. Custom-provider library entries carry `apiMode` because `loadCustomProviders` reads `api_mode` from each `custom_providers:` block.","startLine":45,"endLine":45,"text":"src/main/config.ts#setModelConfig takes an optional apiMode argument, handled exactly like context_length: a non-empty string sets model.api_mode, null/empty removes it (so auto-detection resumes), undefined leaves it untouched. The set-model-config IPC handler (src/main/ipc/register.ts) resolves it from the activated model's apiMode library field (src/main/models.ts#SavedModel) — null when the entry has none — alongside the contextLength mirror, on both the pure-local and remote-fallback local writes. Custom-provider library entries carry apiMode because loadCustomProviders reads api_mode from each custom_providers: block."},{"markdown":"The library lookup runs through [[src/main/ipc/register.ts#resolveLibraryModelEntry]], which disambiguates by base URL when several entries share the same provider+model — e.g. two `custom` endpoints exposing the same model id over different transports. A bare provider+model match would return the first entry and persist its `api_mode` for the other endpoint, routing it over the wrong protocol; matching the base URL too keeps each endpoint's transport correct. Single-entry activations are unaffected.","startLine":47,"endLine":47,"text":"The library lookup runs through src/main/ipc/register.ts#resolveLibraryModelEntry, which disambiguates by base URL when several entries share the same provider+model — e.g. two custom endpoints exposing the same model id over different transports. A bare provider+model match would return the first entry and persist its api_mode for the other endpoint, routing it over the wrong protocol; matching the base URL too keeps each endpoint's transport correct. Single-entry activations are unaffected."},{"markdown":"Each card's logo is resolved by [[src/renderer/src/components/common/BrandLogo.tsx]] from the provider id, falling back to a generic robot for unknown ids.","startLine":51,"endLine":51,"text":"Each card's logo is resolved by src/renderer/src/components/common/BrandLogo.tsx from the provider id, falling back to a generic robot for unknown ids."},{"markdown":"`detectBrand` matches the provider/model string to a `BrandKey`, and `matchTheme` flattens every logo to a single white/black tint so colored and `currentColor` SVGs render uniformly in the grid's logo tiles.","startLine":53,"endLine":53,"text":"detectBrand matches the provider/model string to a BrandKey, and matchTheme flattens every logo to a single white/black tint so colored and currentColor SVGs render uniformly in the grid's logo tiles."},{"markdown":"The Local/Remote preset chips are also branded: each renders the same `BrandLogo` (by preset id) to the left of its name in a row. `llama.cpp` is mapped off the Meta logo to the generic API mark (the `/llama/` substring would otherwise tag it, and Ollama, as Meta); any preset without a bundled logo falls back to the generic mark.","startLine":55,"endLine":55,"text":"The Local/Remote preset chips are also branded: each renders the same BrandLogo (by preset id) to the left of its name in a row. llama.cpp is mapped off the Meta logo to the generic API mark (the /llama/ substring would otherwise tag it, and Ollama, as Meta); any preset without a bundled logo falls back to the generic mark."},{"markdown":"When live OAuth discovery is unavailable, MiniMax keeps a usable model list aligned with Hermes Agent's curated OAuth choices.","startLine":59,"endLine":59,"text":"When live OAuth discovery is unavailable, MiniMax keeps a usable model list aligned with Hermes Agent's curated OAuth choices."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/model-discovery.ts#discoverProviderModels]] falls back to `MiniMax-M3`, `MiniMax-M2.7`, and `MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed` if the Python query fails. Regression coverage preserves all three entries; successful live discovery still takes precedence.","startLine":61,"endLine":61,"text":"src/main/model-discovery.ts#discoverProviderModels falls back to MiniMax-M3, MiniMax-M2.7, and MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed if the Python query fails. Regression coverage preserves all three entries; successful live discovery still takes precedence."},{"markdown":"Novita is available as a remote OpenAI-compatible preset, with a dedicated API-key field and the same endpoint used by Hermes Agent.","startLine":65,"endLine":65,"text":"Novita is available as a remote OpenAI-compatible preset, with a dedicated API-key field and the same endpoint used by Hermes Agent."},{"markdown":"The desktop stores the model as `custom` at `https://api.novita.ai/openai/v1`. Setup, the configured-provider picker, installer readiness, and runtime key lookup use `NOVITA_API_KEY`; provider branding identifies the endpoint as NovitaAI. The shared URL mapping is covered alongside the other supported commercial endpoints.","startLine":67,"endLine":67,"text":"The desktop stores the model as custom at https://api.novita.ai/openai/v1. Setup, the configured-provider picker, installer readiness, and runtime key lookup use NOVITA_API_KEY; provider branding identifies the endpoint as NovitaAI. The shared URL mapping is covered alongside the other supported commercial endpoints."},{"markdown":"Auxiliary credentials belong to the selected provider and endpoint. Switching either clears stale task-level secrets and pointers; model-only changes preserve them.","startLine":71,"endLine":71,"text":"Auxiliary credentials belong to the selected provider and endpoint. Switching either clears stale task-level secrets and pointers; model-only changes preserve them."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/auxiliary-config.ts#setAuxiliaryTask]] clears `api_key`, `key_env`, `api_key_env`, legacy `api`, and `api_mode` when the provider or normalized endpoint changes, or routing returns to `auto`. RAZUM keeps this logic independent of upstream's Hermes One named-provider registry.","startLine":73,"endLine":73,"text":"src/main/auxiliary-config.ts#setAuxiliaryTask clears api_key, key_env, api_key_env, legacy api, and api_mode when the provider or normalized endpoint changes, or routing returns to auto. RAZUM keeps this logic independent of upstream's Hermes One named-provider registry."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/auxiliary-config.ts#resetAuxiliaryToAuto]] clears the same overrides for every task. The text editor changes only direct task fields, preserving nested `extra_body`, other tasks, comments, and line endings; unsupported flow mappings fail before writing.","startLine":75,"endLine":75,"text":"src/main/auxiliary-config.ts#resetAuxiliaryToAuto clears the same overrides for every task. The text editor changes only direct task fields, preserving nested extra_body, other tasks, comments, and line endings; unsupported flow mappings fail before writing."},{"markdown":"Switching providers or changing an endpoint removes prior credential aliases and transport overrides so they cannot leak into the next route.","startLine":79,"endLine":79,"text":"Switching providers or changing an endpoint removes prior credential aliases and transport overrides so they cannot leak into the next route."},{"markdown":"Changing the model under the same effective provider and endpoint preserves task-specific credentials and transport settings. Omitted versus explicit native default URLs resolve to the same route.","startLine":83,"endLine":83,"text":"Changing the model under the same effective provider and endpoint preserves task-specific credentials and transport settings. Omitted versus explicit native default URLs resolve to the same route."},{"markdown":"Resetting to the main model persists `auto` routing without stale task-level credentials, while leaving unrelated settings intact after reload.","startLine":87,"endLine":87,"text":"Resetting to the main model persists auto routing without stale task-level credentials, while leaving unrelated settings intact after reload."},{"markdown":"Routing updates and credential removal address direct task children only, preserving nested options, comments, empty task maps, multiline values, and CRLF line endings.","startLine":91,"endLine":91,"text":"Routing updates and credential removal address direct task children only, preserving nested options, comments, empty task maps, multiline values, and CRLF line endings."},{"markdown":"Saved RAZUM custom providers use their model-library name and normalized base URL as the credential identity, without requiring the upstream Hermes One provider registry.","startLine":95,"endLine":95,"text":"Saved RAZUM custom providers use their model-library name and normalized base URL as the credential identity, without requiring the upstream Hermes One provider registry."},{"markdown":"The shared [[src/shared/url-key-map.ts#customProviderEnvKey]] transform maps the saved name to `CUSTOM_PROVIDER_<NAME>_KEY`. Endpoint comparison normalizes scheme and host case, default ports, and trailing slashes while preserving path and query case.","startLine":97,"endLine":97,"text":"The shared src/shared/url-key-map.ts#customProviderEnvKey transform maps the saved name to CUSTOM_PROVIDER_<NAME>_KEY. Endpoint comparison normalizes scheme and host case, default ports, and trailing slashes while preserving path and query case."},{"markdown":"Readiness checks accept a per-name key only when a saved `custom` model matches the active endpoint and the selected profile owns the credential.","startLine":101,"endLine":101,"text":"Readiness checks accept a per-name key only when a saved custom model matches the active endpoint and the selected profile owns the credential."},{"markdown":"The credential may come from the profile environment or its resolved secret provider. A named profile never borrows the default profile's key.","startLine":103,"endLine":103,"text":"The credential may come from the profile environment or its resolved secret provider. A named profile never borrows the default profile's key."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/models.ts#readModelsRaw]] resolves the model-store path at call time so the config-to-models import cycle cannot access `HERMES_HOME` before installer initialization finishes.","startLine":105,"endLine":105,"text":"src/main/models.ts#readModelsRaw resolves the model-store path at call time so the config-to-models import cycle cannot access HERMES_HOME before installer initialization finishes."},{"markdown":"CLI launch applies the same endpoint match, skips matching saved rows whose per-name key is empty, and continues until it finds a usable key in the selected profile environment or enumerated secret provider.","startLine":109,"endLine":109,"text":"CLI launch applies the same endpoint match, skips matching saved rows whose per-name key is empty, and continues until it finds a usable key in the selected profile environment or enumerated secret provider."}],"blocks":[{"type":"heading","start":0,"end":16,"startLine":1,"endLine":1,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":18,"end":267,"startLine":3,"endLine":3,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":269,"end":532,"startLine":5,"endLine":5,"children":[]},{"type":"heading","start":534,"end":562,"startLine":7,"endLine":7,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":564,"end":728,"startLine":9,"endLine":9,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":730,"end":1117,"startLine":11,"endLine":11,"children":[]},{"type":"heading","start":1119,"end":1167,"startLine":13,"endLine":13,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":1169,"end":1320,"startLine":15,"endLine":15,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":1322,"end":1813,"startLine":17,"endLine":17,"children":[]},{"type":"heading","start":1815,"end":1865,"startLine":19,"endLine":19,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":1867,"end":2075,"startLine":21,"endLine":21,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":2077,"end":2379,"startLine":23,"endLine":23,"children":[]},{"type":"heading","start":2381,"end":2443,"startLine":25,"endLine":25,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":2445,"end":2672,"startLine":27,"endLine":27,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":2674,"end":3033,"startLine":29,"endLine":29,"children":[]}